# Per-Dockerfile override (BuildKit convention: <Dockerfile>.dockerignore
# next to the Dockerfile it applies to) for Dockerfile.lildaemon's
# `COPY lildaemon/ .` step. Build context here is Development/ (this
# file's grandparent), so paths below are relative to that root.
#
# data/, output/, and workspace/ are all bind-mounted at runtime
# (docker-compose.yml: ../lildaemon/{data,output,workspace}:/app/...), so
# baking their build-time contents into the image is pure waste — the
# mount shadows them at container start regardless. Confirmed live on
# pineal 2026-09-18: workspace/ had accumulated 1.6GB of unrelated
# leftover data (stray dagda fastText model binaries) that got copied
# into every rebuilt image and filled the host's disk.
lildaemon/data/
lildaemon/output/
lildaemon/workspace/

# Never needed in the image: dependencies come from pip install, not a
# local venv; git history has no runtime purpose.
lildaemon/.venv/
lildaemon/.git/

# Secrets never belong in an image layer. The repo's .env (gitignored, never committed) holds API keys,
# tokens and JWT secrets; it used to be copied in by `COPY lildaemon/ .` and loaded at import by
# goat/__init__.py's load_dotenv(), so a variable NOT set in docker-compose.yml silently fell back to a
# value from that hidden file (found 2026-09-21: an unconfigured EDGEQUAKE_BASE_URL let the
# assistant-documents reaper run in a second FieryPit). Configuration reaches the container through
# compose `environment:` only. Measured before excluding it: the only variables the live container got
# solely from the baked file were CLIPS_MCP_URL, FIERYPIT_BASE_URL, GITHUB_TOKEN, GROQ_BASE_URL,
# OLLAMA_URL and PROLOG_MCP_URL, and none is read in a way compose does not already cover.
lildaemon/.env
lildaemon/.env.*
lildaemon/**/.env
